# ...but the committed template is the one exception — see the `!.` line below.
# Without it the `.env*` glob swallows .env.example, and both the README's
# `cp .env.example .env.local` and the runtime hint in src/lib/supabase.ts
# would point at a file that can never exist.
!.env.example
supabase/.temp/
dev_server_run.log
dev_server_err.log
dev.log
docs/diagrams/*.html

# local build/verify output dumps
tsc_out.txt
vitest_out.txt

# local APK downloads from CI artifacts
*.apk
android/app/yatraflow-debug.p12
dev-5174.log

# local agent skills (project-local installs). `.claude/` itself stays
# un-ignored so committed editor config remains possible.
.agents/
.claude/skills/
skills-lock.json

# Agent-tool working directories and generated briefs — regenerateable output,
# never repo content, and never worth a conflict between two branches.
# `.impeccable/browser/` alone is a full browser profile (12 MB); `PRODUCT.md`
# carries the skill's own schema marker rather than being a hand-written product
# doc; `.freebuff/` and `.cache/` hold tool state and probe/log dumps — the
# latter is why `vite.config.ts` pins the vitest `include` (stale copies of this
# repo turn up under these trees and the gate used to fail on their months-old
# tests). `.cache/` was covered only by a local `.git/info/exclude`, which does
# not travel with a clone.
.impeccable/
.commandcode/
.freebuff/
.cache/
.dsh/
PRODUCT.md

# Lane handoff notes (`HANDOFF-DSH-LANE-A-MAP.md` and its siblings). They are
# clone-local coordination documents between agent sessions: they name absolute
# Windows paths and the working tree they were written against, which must never
# be tracked in a public repo, and each clone keeps its own. Anchored to the root
# so a future `docs/handoff-*.md` stays committable.
/HANDOFF-*.md

# The Verdent agent's PR-body scratch file — same class a third time. It held a
# whole PR body (10 KB of prose), and every branch that used the tool rewrote
# it, so two of them could never stay open together without conflicting on it.
# `.verdentc.json` is deliberately NOT ignored: that one is real deploy config
# (install/build commands, output dir), not tool output.
.verdent/

# The Superdesign design-tool working directory - same class as the block above:
# its `init/` context is regenerated from source by the skill, its `tmp/` holds the
# Petite-Vue component HTML waiting on `create-component`, and neither is repo
# content. `tmp/` must be ignored per the skill's own SOP so generated HTML is
# never committed; `init/` is ignored with it because a second agent working this
# clone must not see six new untracked analysis files in `git status`, and because
# ignoring the directory does not affect the skill - it reads them from disk.
.superdesign/

# Our own transient `gh pr create --body-file` scratch — the same class as the
# Verdent block above: regenerated per PR, rewritten by every branch that uses
# it, never repo content. It slipped into one commit only while the mavis-trash
# launcher was stale; ignored so it can never recur.
.pr-body.md
